    },
    {
      "name": "node02.text",
      "source_pointer": "/body/1/text",
      "kind": "string",
      "synthetic_source_example": "On day one the controller opens a single exceptions queue instead of a stack of spreadsheets. Each item shows the account, the amount, the likely cause and the person who owns the fix."
    },
    {
      "name": "node03.text",
      "source_pointer": "/body/2/text",
      "kind": "string",
      "synthetic_source_example": "By the end of day two most items are cleared by the entity accountants. What remains are judgment calls: a reserve, a reclassification, a timing question. Those are the items a controller should spend time on."
    },
    {
      "name": "node04.text",
      "source_pointer": "/body/3/text",
      "kind": "string",
      "synthetic_source_example": "Nothing waits for the end of the month to be looked at, so nothing arrives all at once."
    },
    {
      "name": "node06.text",
      "source_pointer": "/body/5/text",
      "kind": "string",
      "synthetic_source_example": "Note"
    },
    {
      "name": "node07.text",
      "source_pointer": "/body/6/text",
      "kind": "string",
      "synthetic_source_example": "Pilot entities cleared exceptions in two days on average, against nine days before the pilot."
    }
